description:
On prod, the published manual post (seed_kind=manual, chunks_used=[]) carries its CITATIONS block on a SINGLE line: 'CITATIONS: [trad | text | section | TIER: verified] [..] [..]'. parseCitationsBlock finds the marker via /^[^\S
]*CITATIONS:[^
]*$/m, but marker[0] consumes the whole line (the [^
]* eats every bracket entry). It then scans only text.slice(marker.index + marker[0].length).split('
') for entries — which is empty. Net: body gets the block stripped, zero citations parse, Sources section disappears (regression introduced by PR #91 / todo:a0e98810; pre-#91 the raw block at least rendered as plaintext). Fix: scan the whole block region (from marker to EOF) for [..] groups regardless of newlines, preserving line-based optional quote attachment. Add regression test with the inline format. Repro post slug: state-of-the-atlas-the-spine-is-genealogy-the-surprise-is-the-tao.
